WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410
Two messages arrive about Pablo.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.350
The first says: Pablo es aburrido.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.650
The second says: Pablo está aburrido.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.910
Same Pablo.

5
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.090
Same adjective.

6
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.150
Both verbs mean "is".

7
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.190
Yet Pablo would be much happier
to read one of them than the

8
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:16.910
other.

9
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.930
So which one would upset him, and why?

10
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.910
In this mission, you'll meet the
two Spanish verbs for "to be":

11
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.680
ser and estar.

12
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.330
You'll sort the jobs each one does,

13
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.450
from telling the time to
saying where a city is.

14
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.230
And you'll see how swapping
the verb can change what an

15
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.710
adjective means.

16
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.290
Your mission: work out which
message Pablo would rather not

17
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.350
read.
